"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative launched with a kick-off on June 15th, led by Sarah Tan, with an initial phase one budget of $500,000. The team expanded in September with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule. Phase two has achieved a breakthrough in predictive analytics, with a detailed report scheduled for the November 20th staff meeting. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. Additionally, the compliance plan budget was increased to $55,000, and security protocols (including multi-factor authentication and encryption) will be updated effective January next year. A celebration for the testing milestone is planned for October 10th."
